SDUSD::mint
├── given PAUSE_TYPE or FROZEN_TYPE is active
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused
└── given neither PAUSE_TYPE nor FROZEN_TYPE is active
    ├── when receiver is zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ERC20InvalidReceiver
    ├── when caller has insufficient DUSD balance or allowance
    │   ├── it should revert with the underlying token transfer error
    │   └── it should leave accounted assets, deposit cap usage, and share supply unchanged
    ├── when requested shares exceeds maxMint for receiver
    │   ├── it should revert with ERC4626ExceededMaxMint
    │   └── it should leave deposit cap usage and vault state unchanged
    ├── when total supply is zero
    │   ├── when receiver is address(1) and assets and shares equal seedShares
    │   │   ├── it should accept the seed mint
    │   │   ├── it should exclude the seed from depositCapUsage
    │   │   ├── it should mint all shares to address(1)
    │   │   └── it should emit Deposit
    │   ├── when receiver is not address(1)
    │   │   └── it should revert with ERC4626ExceededMaxMint because maxMint is zero
    │   ├── when receiver is address(1) and shares is below seedShares
    │   │   └── it should revert with SDUSDInvalidSeedDeposit
    │   └── when receiver is address(1) and shares exceeds seedShares
    │       └── it should revert with ERC4626ExceededMaxMint
    └── when total supply is non-zero
        ├── it should calculate required assets by rounding up
        ├── it should transfer required assets from caller to the vault
        ├── it should increase accountedAssets by required assets
        ├── it should increase depositCapUsage by required assets
        ├── it should mint the requested shares to receiver
        ├── it should leave the seed share balance unchanged
        ├── it should return the required asset amount
        ├── it should emit Deposit
        ├── it should not decrease the exchange rate because required assets round up in favor of the vault
        ├── when requested shares is zero
        │   ├── it should complete without changing accounting or balances
        │   ├── it should leave depositCapUsage unchanged
        │   ├── it should emit Deposit with zero assets and shares
        │   └── it should preserve the exchange rate
        ├── when a reward period is active
        │   ├── it should price the mint using only currently unlocked assets
        │   ├── released rewards should consume capacity and the mint should add its required assets
        │   └── it should not decrease the exchange rate when required assets round up
        ├── when requested shares equals maxMint
        │   ├── it should accept the mint
        │   └── required assets should not exceed the remaining DUSD headroom
        └── when the vault has received a raw DUSD donation
            ├── it should ignore the donation when calculating required assets
            ├── it should leave the exchange rate unchanged before the mint
            └── it should not decrease the exchange rate when required assets round up
